@essay rh="THE PARISH HOUSEHOLD · LEAH · THE MACHINERY AROUND HER"
# The machinery around her
drop: Leah lives inside the system the Trials sit on top of. A Commonwife is a registration status (FR 1), assessed quarterly in Aurem by a Vowed officer who notices when two years pass without a pregnancy (MEN). Her husband was given a wife and told what to expect, and the Empire built no way for her to say she isn't ready (MEN).
Above her, Aurem itself made marriage look like the highest honor a woman can get, on purpose (DOM). Behind her is a mother who lived the same registration and was moved to another man's house when her husband left (FR 0). In front of her, every evening at seven, is her sister's score (TR).
side:
chips: MEN, DOM, FR 0–1
k: The clock
stext: Two years and counting. What happens after Temple review is still yours to decide (Vol. I, {v1:household-q}).
marg
see: Vol. I, Commonwives, {v1:arrangement}.
/end

@page rh="THE PARISH HOUSEHOLD · LEAH AND ZION · BOTH SIDES" m="TKC: MEN"
# Leah and Zion
They sit at Celeste's table and don't talk about the things they can't talk about, and the not-talking is its own communication (MEN). He misses her in a way he has no words for and carries it as anger (MEN).
